      "urpx:forRatePlanModifier": {
        "@id": "sce:care"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "sce:cc-care-2026-03-20",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "sce:cc-care-2026-03-20-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "Sheet 1 of Schedule D-CARE states a 32.5 percent discount applied to a CARE customer's bill prior to the Public Utilities Commission Reimbursement Fee and any applicable user fees, taxes and late payment charges. This filing models it as a urpx:Price carrying urpx:multiplier -0.325 over the discountable subtotal of whichever SCE residential base plan the customer takes service under. The price names the candidate subtotals of four schedules at every effective date, read disjunctively so that the one present in the consumer's graph applies. Those subtotals are defined by the base filings rather than by this one; each holds the per-kWh charges of its plan, from thirteen on Schedule D to twenty-four on TOU-D-PRIME at this date, and each omits the Reimbursement Fee by the sentence above, the California Climate Credit, which Special Condition 12 applies after city and county utility users' taxes, and the Base Services Charge, which this filing instead adjusts through two per-meter-per-day credits. The four line items of the same Sheet 1 are carried alongside the percentage: the Wildfire Fund Non-Bypassable Charge exemption of $0.00591 per kWh, the Fixed Recovery Charge exemption of $0.00619 per kWh, the Base Services Charge Surcharge exemption of $0.064 per meter per day, and the Base Services Charge Discount of $(0.155) per meter per day. Three benefits of the schedule remain unrepresented, and they are why this claim is partial. Sheet 1 exempts CARE customers from the CARE Surcharge of $0.208 per meter per day, which no SCE residential rate sheet in this corpus itemizes, so that exemption has no base charge to cancel. Special Condition 14 grants the San Joaquin Valley Disadvantaged Communities Pilot Bill Protection Discount, 20 percent in pilot years 1 through 5 and 10 or 20 percent in years 6 through 10, and Special Condition 15 a 20 percent Transitional Community Solar Discount; both are limited to pilot participants, and this filing carries no condition on pilot participation to gate them on. Several other Special Conditions are out of scope rather than missing: the CARE Household income test of Special Condition 2, the application, commencement, verification and notice rules of Special Conditions 4, 5, 7 and 8, the rebilling of Special Condition 9, and the Arrearage Management Plan debt forgiveness of Special Condition 13 are eligibility and account administration rather than rates. The California Climate Credit of Special Condition 12 is carried on the base rate plans this modifier overlays.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-09-21T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
